> > get overexposed.
>
> These were meant as a joke.  However, your point about the papere golem
> YAFM being overexposed is a good one.  I'll have to consider this when
> thinking about new YAFMs.

Cool, cool.  By way of examples, there's a special message the game
gives if you're poly'd into a metalvore and eat a trident, there's a
special message if a pit viper falls into a pit trap, and there's a
special message if you die in the very first turn of a game.  Consider
those to be about the rarity needed for a successful Nethack joke --
they should be something a player encounters after his thousandth game
and makes him wonder that's there's still stuff he hasn't seen yet, not
something that makes the player groan to himself because he's seen it
each of those thousand times before.


