> > > [18]: Failing to successfully over enchant armor, rings and weapons
> > > (meaning the item was vaporized) should abuse wisdom. (Rings and
> > > weapons suggested by SpeedEvi1) --aristotle73
> >
> > Not logical.  It can be wise to make the attempt if you already have
> > another +7 weapon.  It's unlucky, not necessarily unwise.
>
> If the armor vibrates, it is a sign that further enchanting is
> dangerous.  I'll have to think about this a little more.

Dangerous, yes, but possibly an acceptable risk.  The player doesn't
know going in if it'll evaporate the item or not, so the act isn't
universally bad.  If he's already got another +7 weapon, it's probably
worth it.

In other words, wisdom should only be exercised or abused concerning
things the player has real control over, not the results of random die
rolls.

